Original commit body from 3433f1783153483dcf64e142c7b80e336d43a8f9:

Addresses WI-fukaf. The linker treated Symbol.path as absolute, but the
pipeline hands it repo-relative paths ('src/a.ts'). Two effects:

(a) Relative imports resolved against the process CWD, so a survey run from
    outside the repository lost links. Every bakeoff runs that way.
(b) tsconfig `paths` aliases never resolved from any directory: the ancestor
    walk compared 'src' with the index's absolute keys. Each import minted a
    phantom npm package instead (typescript:npm:0-0:@/lib:package).

The source path is now `repo_root.resolve() / src_path` for both lookups (an
absolute path is unchanged), and relative_to uses the resolved root. This is
how vue_component.py already did it.

Measured, dev 300780b5bf (pinned worktree) vs this branch, surveyed from
outside the repo:
  koel      imports 3,680 -> 4,078, module_exports 1,471 -> 2,085; the fix
            gives the identical edge set from inside the repo.
  full-stack-fastapi-template  imports 301 -> 411, module_exports 0 -> 288;
            the five @/... phantom npm packages are gone.
  nest      imports 2,587 -> 4,033, module_exports 0 -> 1,981; the in-repo
            @nestjs/* packages the root tsconfig maps to ./packages/* are no
            longer npm nodes.
Tests use repo-relative paths from a foreign cwd: a direct linker test, and
a production survey from inside vs outside that must agree. The survey test
reproduces the phantom on the old code.

